 to be possible and what actually was.", "last_comment_created": 1786230595579, "content": "", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": true, "comments": 0, "score_up": 32, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"status": 200}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "text", "uuid": "1ATCE0sqYO", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 23, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "apu", "id": 8770784, "raw_content": "I think Matt Walsh put it best when he coined the phrase \"Israel First, from the Other Direction\" - a term that refers to people who are Israel First, but from the angle of prioritizing or supporting anything that's anti-Israel no matter what.\n\nAmong the clearest signs of this I've seen most recently are people who are arguing in support of the International Criminal Court, a corrupt, weak, unelected globalist organization that the US has explicitly rejected to such a degree that not even the likes of Bill Clinton or Barack Obama tried to make the US a member.\n\nThe same ICC that it was recently declared the US is working to destroy because the ICC is trying to charge US citizens for their work protecting the border.\n\nYet because the ICC has an arrest warrant out for the Prime Minister of Israel, somehow the ICC is a good thing and \"Israel First, from the Other Direction\" crowd are all too happy to be pro-globalist so long as globalism supports their own personal agenda.\n\nIt's not enough to find *actual* criticisms of Israel and rely on those; no, if the ICC has targeted Israel, then apparently the ICC has to be treated as legitimate in spite of being part of the very globalist agenda that also wants to destroy the United States.\n\nIt's all so frustrating...", "author": "AmericanJawa", "created": 1786237046568, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "AmericanJawa", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_source": "", "link": "", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "'Israel Derangement Syndrome' is so bad it has people defending globalism as long as globalism lets them complain about Israel.", "last_comment_created": 1786250870355, "content": "<p>I think Matt Walsh put it best when he coined the phrase &quot;Israel First, from the Other Direction&quot; - a term that refers to people who are Israel First, but from the angle of prioritizing or supporting anything that's anti-Israel no matter what.</p>\n<p>Among the clearest signs of this I've seen most recently are people who are arguing in support of the International Criminal Court, a corrupt, weak, unelected globalist organization that the US has explicitly rejected to such a degree that not even the likes of Bill Clinton or Barack Obama tried to make the US a member.</p>\n<p>The same ICC that it was recently declared the US is working to destroy because the ICC is trying to charge US citizens for their work protecting the border.</p>\n<p>Yet because the ICC has an arrest warrant out for the Prime Minister of Israel, somehow the ICC is a good thing and &quot;Israel First, from the Other Direction&quot; crowd are all too happy to be pro-globalist so long as globalism supports their own personal agenda.</p>\n<p>It's not enough to find <em>actual</em> criticisms of Israel and rely on those; no, if the ICC has targeted Israel, then apparently the ICC has to be treated as legitimate in spite of being part of the very globalist agenda that also wants to destroy the United States.</p>\n<p>It's all so frustrating...</p>\n", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "i